### 3a. Holdings — migrate, don't forward (owner, 2026-09-13)

Instead of an IONOS forward, **`fishboneholdings.co.uk` moves off 1&1 and is added as a secondary
domain in Construction's Google Workspace** — the "Construction hub" consolidation already scoped in
Eugene's `Runbook-Workspace-Consolidation-into-Construction.md`. This is a **staged domain migration**,
not a settings toggle: confirm the super-admin, add the secondary domain, verify domain ownership,
cut MX/DNS to Google, provision `info@fishboneholdings.co.uk` in the tenant, and IMAP-migrate existing
mail off 1&1. Once done, `info@fishboneholdings.co.uk` is a mailbox **in the same tenant as the hub**,
so it routes with a simple internal Gmail forward (like Construction's own addresses).

**Consequence for sequencing:** the other five entities route **now** via simple forwards; **Holdings
joins after the migration**. The group inbox can go live for five first and gain Holdings when the
migration completes — the build is not blocked on it. **SSAS stays on 1&1 and is excluded** (§5); its
own migration is a separate infra question, not needed for Peter routing.

